######## 0. BASELINE (unpatched semantics: no BS52): compile only vs run, lib missing
$ BS52=off ERL_LIBS=<unset> bsc Probe 
    exit=0
$ BS52=off ERL_LIBS=<unset> bsc Probe Shout "hi"
    crashed: error:undef
    exit=1
######## 1. module-presence check, no new syntax (BS52=module)
$ BS52=module ERL_LIBS=<unset> bsc Probe 
    Probe/probe.bs:3: error: module 'Elixir.String' is not on the code path
      `using :'Elixir.String'` promises it; nothing here says which application provides it.
    exit=1
$ BS52=module ERL_LIBS=/tmp/otp/lib/elixir/lib bsc Probe Shout "hi"
    "HI"
    exit=0
######## 2. app named, correct (BS52=app)
$ BS52=app ERL_LIBS=<unset> bsc Probe 
    Probe/probe.bs:3: error: application 'elixir' (declared for module 'Elixir.String') is not on the code path
      put its directory on ERL_LIBS, or fix the name after `in`.
    exit=1
$ BS52=app ERL_LIBS=/tmp/otp/lib/elixir/lib bsc Probe Shout "hi"
    "HI"
    exit=0
######## 3. app named, WRONG application (module lives in elixir, declared eex)
$ BS52=app ERL_LIBS=/tmp/otp/lib/elixir/lib bsc Probe Shout "hi"
    Probe/probe.bs:3: error: module 'Elixir.String' resolves to /tmp/otp/lib/elixir/lib/elixir/ebin/Elixir.String.beam, outside application 'eex' (/tmp/otp/lib/elixir/lib/eex)
    exit=1
######## 4. app named, application absent (req), module present elsewhere
$ BS52=app ERL_LIBS=/tmp/otp/lib/elixir/lib bsc Probe Shout "hi"
    Probe/probe.bs:3: error: application 'req' (declared for module 'Elixir.String') is not on the code path
      put its directory on ERL_LIBS, or fix the name after `in`.
    exit=1
######## 5. false positive: module reachable by bare -pa (no app dir), app check refuses
$ BS52=module  erl -pa bare  (module check)
    "HI"
$ BS52=app     erl -pa bare  (app check)
    Probe/probe.bs:3: error: application 'elixir' (declared for module 'Elixir.String') is not on the code path
      put its directory on ERL_LIBS, or fix the name after `in`.
